# Always push after updates

When you finish implementing or fixing something in this project:

1. Stage the relevant files. Never stage `.env`, credentials, or uploaded documents.
2. Create a git commit if there are changes.
3. Push to `origin` on the current branch (`git push -u origin HEAD` if the branch has no upstream).

Do this without being asked again. Do not force-push. Do not skip hooks.
